  "result": "I fixed two bugs in `src/`, and `npm test` now passes all 243 tests. I didn't change the tests.\n\n1. **Discount and tax were applied in the wrong order** (`src/cart.js`). The code added tax first and then took the discount off. The comment in that file and the tests both say the discount comes off the subtotal before tax. I swapped the order, so a $100 subtotal with a $20 discount and 10% tax now gives (100 − 20) × 1.1 = **$88**. Before, it gave $90.\n2. **Fixed discounts could push the total below zero** (`src/discount.js`). A $20 discount on a $5 item came out to −14.5. The fixed-discount result is now clamped with `Math.max(0, …)`, so it stops at zero. Percent discounts don't need this because the allowed range is 0–100%.\n\nThe 240 percent-discount tests were already passing because the order doesn't matter for those: taking a percentage off and adding a percentage of tax give the same result either way round.",
